  "question": {
    "text": "pH of water is 7 at $25^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$. If water is heated to $80^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$., it's pH will :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "7ta0J",
      "text": "Decrease",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "lZ2ZK",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{H}^{+}$concentration increases, $\\mathrm{OH}^{-}$concentration decreases",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "alD5U",
      "text": "Remains the same",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "RNwVW",
      "text": "Increase",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "At $25^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$, pure water has $\\mathrm{pH}=7$\nAs temperature increased, water molecules dissociate more into hydrogen ions ( $\\mathrm{H}^{+}$) and hydroxide ions $\\left(\\mathrm{OH}^{-}\\right)$.\nThis increased dissociation leads to slightly decrease in pH .\nAt $80^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}, \\mathrm{pH} \\approx 6.93$",
    "image": null
  },
